description:
Create a monitor on its first check-in. The same slug uses the same monitor. Service and billing limits apply. A rejected creation writes no monitor or event. The slug becomes the monitor name and its identity: the same slug always means the same monitor, so a retry never creates a second one. Normalised to lowercase, `[a-z0-9-]`, 40 chars. Creation happens **only inside the free tier** (or the trial); past it the ping is a 402 with `accepts[]` and nothing is written — not even the event. Works by GET or POST. Returns: { ok, endpoint_id, created }
Example: curl -fsS "$ORIGIN/in/$INGEST_KEY/nightly-backup?cron=0%203%20*%20*%20*&tz=UTC&grace_sec=900"
Errors: 400: `slug_invalido` — nothing usable left after normalising. With `cron`: `cron_invalido`, `tz_invalida`, `grace_invalido` or `cron_sem_ocorrencia`.; 402: The free tier is full: pay and repeat, or delete a monitor.; 404: Unknown or rotated ingest key.
